{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1: Copilot session read",
  "description": "End-to-end: how launching the desktop app turns on-disk Copilot telemetry into rows in the Sessions view. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "isPrimary": true,
  "nextTour": "2: Session detail & token trend",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Fork the data host",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/main/index.ts",
      "line": 127,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-1.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Dev → Electron main: Launch the app`**\n\nLaunching the app runs `startDataHost`, which forks the data host as an Electron `utilityProcess`. Every read, parse and index pass happens there — off the main process and out of the renderer — and the read-only, privacy-first pipeline starts: nothing leaves the machine."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — Connect the renderer to the data host",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/main/index.ts",
      "line": 141,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-2.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Electron main → Sessions view: hand over a MessagePort`**\n\n`connectRendererToDataHost` creates a `MessageChannelMain` and gives one end to the data host and the other to the page (the preload transfers it with `window.postMessage`). From then on the two talk directly; main is out of the path entirely."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — The index pass runs each source",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/background/worker.ts",
      "line": 114,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-3.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Data host → CopilotIndexer: background index pass`**\n\nThe data host's background worker runs one indexer per enabled source in turn; for Copilot that is `CopilotIndexer.run()`. The renderer never waits on this pass — rows stream in as they are found."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Read-only open",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/indexer/copilotIndexer.ts",
      "line": 215,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-4.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotIndexer → Copilot DB: read-only open`**\n\nCopilot's database is somebody else's live file, so it is opened `readonly` with `fileMustExist`: it is never created, migrated or written. A candidate that cannot be opened is reported and skipped, without hiding the others."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — One consistent read",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/indexer/copilotIndexer.ts",
      "line": 234,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-5.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Copilot DB → CopilotIndexer: session aggregates`**\n\nAll summaries for a source are read inside one `db.transaction`, so they describe the same SQLite snapshot even while Copilot keeps committing spans. Only per-session aggregates come back — counts, durations, token totals — never raw prompt or completion text."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Upsert into the local index",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/indexer/copilotIndexer.ts",
      "line": 316,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-6.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `CopilotIndexer → IndexDb: upsertChangedSessions(rows)`**\n\nThe rows land in the app's own `IndexDb`, and only rows that actually changed are reported through `onRows`. The data host re-emits those as a `sessions.upserted` event, so an open list patches in place instead of re-querying."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 7 — The view asks for a page",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/renderer/src/views/sessions/useSessions.ts",
      "line": 127,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-7.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 7 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Sessions view → Data host: sessions.list`**\n\nThe Sessions view's `useSessions` hook calls `dataHost.call('sessions.list', ...)` over the port. The view holds no data of its own; it always pulls a page from the data host on demand."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 8 — Query the index",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/datahost/indexer/indexDb.ts",
      "line": 511,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-8.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 8 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `Data host → IndexDb: IndexDb.listSessions()`**\n\n`IndexDb.listSessions` answers from the local index — filters, hidden sessions and the rename/tag overlays applied in SQL — so listing never opens Copilot's database at all. The data host decorates the rows and returns them."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 9 — Paint the session list",
      "file": "src/desktop/agent-observability-desktop/src/renderer/src/views/sessions/SessionsView.tsx",
      "line": 369,
      "description": "![1: Copilot session read](.tours/diagrams/d-9.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 9 of 9 in the sequence diagram — `IndexDb → Sessions view: SessionRow[]`**\n\nFinally the view renders each row as a `SessionRowItem` inside a virtualized list, and the Sessions panel paints. The loop stays lazy: the next index pass pushes only the rows that changed."
    }
  ]
}
